            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "$\\sqrt{5}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Irrational, $2.24$.",
              "worked": "$\\sqrt{5}\\approx2.24$ (2 d.p.). It is irrational because 5 is not a perfect square.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q8-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$18\\%$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Rational, $0.18$.",
              "worked": "$18\\%=\\frac{18}{100}=0.18$. It is rational because it can be written as a fraction of integers.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q8-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$\\frac{2}{5}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Rational, $0.40$.",
              "worked": "$\\frac{2}{5}=0.4=0.40$ (2 d.p.). It is rational because it is a fraction of integers.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q8-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$-124\\%$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Rational, $-1.24$.",
              "worked": "$-124\\%=\\frac{-124}{100}=-1.24$. It is rational because it can be written as a fraction of integers.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q8-e",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": "$1\\frac{5}{7}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Rational, $1.71$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1\\frac{5}{7}&=\\frac{12}{7}\\\\&=1.\\overline{714285}\\\\&\\approx1.71\\quad\\text{(2 d.p.)}\\end{align*}$$ It is rational because it is a fraction of integers; its decimal repeats.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q8-f",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "$-\\sqrt{2}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Irrational, $-1.41$.",
              "worked": "$-\\sqrt{2}\\approx-1.41$ (2 d.p.). Since $\\sqrt{2}$ is irrational, its negative is also irrational.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q8-g",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "g",
            "prompt": "$2\\sqrt{3}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Irrational, $3.46$.",
              "worked": "$2\\sqrt{3}\\approx3.46$ (2 d.p.). Multiplying the irrational number $\\sqrt{3}$ by 2 gives an irrational number.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q8-h",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "h",
            "prompt": "$\\pi$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Irrational, $3.14$.",
              "worked": "$\\pi\\approx3.14$ (2 d.p.). Its decimal is non-terminating and non-recurring, so it is irrational.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          }
        ]
      },
